{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407723-setting-shattering-accomplishments","id":1407723,"title":"Setting shattering accomplishments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-12T10:30:26-07:00","id":1407723,"title":"Setting shattering accomplishments","content":"What are some of the things that either your character, your players did, or your ST did in an Exalted game that shattered major setting precepts? Someone that fit well and made your group, but if you try to advocate it being part of the core setting people would look at you as if you were crazy. Major things that shatter the very precepts of the game itself. The intention isn't to shit on others ideas or stories, but rather share them and ask &quot;How the hell did that happen?&quot;<br /> <br /> Here are a few I've heard of and some ways to start off.<ul><li>Morke's example of his circle using Time Travel to head back in time</li> <li>A story of a 2e game where a Twilight managed to unlock the secrets of Exaltations and learn how to make her own champions.</li> <li>A Raksha player who wanted the biggest harem in Creation, to the point where he successfully infiltrated heaven and made all Exaltations seek females only.</li> <li>An ST I saw who declared that 90% of Dragonblooded are women. He gave some interesting points to how such a thing would work out too.</li> <li>An early 2e game a friend had saw them &quot;defeat&quot; the Wyld and beat all the Raksha by using the Imperial Manse to Wyld shape infinity. This made Creation itself into an infinite plane.</li> <li>A Storyteller that gave my Twilight the weapon who belonged to her First Age self after appeasing it's ghost: An Artifact NA daiklave called Horizon Clever. It allowed melee attacks a range, had infinite range, and was even capable of cutting the distance between two points for faster travel. It could even cut reality and allow one to enter other planes of existance (Yu-Shan, Underworld, etc). Thank god we managed to appease the ghost no violently as if the ghost was using that thing then things would've gotten... really ugly.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T12:21:16-07:00","id":1407751,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>The PCs discovered that their ancestors had created a country where the Incarnae have no sway. The Zenith had convinced the Celestials (and the Eclipse sanctified the oath) to never exalt anyone inside the area and not to intervene directly in that place.</li> <li>The PCs travelled to a land where Fair Folk lived freely alongside mortals within Creation. These Fair Folk had learned to sustain themselves solely on ambient emotions and therefore could survive without eating people's souls.</li> <li>A campaign's ultimate villain was a Solar who had siphoned his 4 Circlemates' Castes to become a 5 Castes superbeing.</li> <li>A Twilight and their Changing Moon mate changed their Caste by attuning to each other's Caste - The Twilight used the Changing Moon's Essence to become more social, turning into a Zenith, while the Changing Moon used the Twilight's essence to become more scholarly, turning into a No Moon.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:01:18-07:00","id":1407774,"title":"","content":"Biggest accomplishment is probably storing a backup copy of Creation in the Loom of Fate, then using the Sword of Creation to destroy all of Creation and rebuild it from the stored backup, with some minor tweaks. <br /> <br /> Conquered the entire East in an empire forged by Solars, but speedran the Usurpation by making any Lunars and Dragonblooded firmly subservient to any Solars, which ended up overturning the whole thing and shattering it into pieces.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve also seen The Ebon Dragon slain in a single attack about a half dozen times. Killing a primordial in one blow is pretty baller stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:49:44-07:00","id":1407799,"title":"","content":"*deep breath*<br /> <br /> The son of a Solar Night and Chosen of Serenity is sought after by Abyssals, Infernals, Sidereals, and a Solar circle (the players, which the Night caste is a part of) as the child is part of a prophecy with multiple interpretations. Eventually they find him and kill his 3rd circle demon keeper, who's death triggers a transformation and the child matures and has strange powers that are demonic, Solar, and Sidereal in nature. The child is convinced their purpose is to go open the door to Heaven for the Infernals (triggering the Lotus Massacre and the Reclamation, in accordance with the prophecy) and the circle had to wrestle with killing the child or letting them go.<br /> <br /> The Zenith sacrifices his Grand Daiklaive (a dangerous weapon sought after by Heaven with the power to permanently sever threads of the Loom of Fate and a plot point from the start of the game) to the Unconquered Sun for advice. UCS tells him that Fate is set but the Exalted make their own fate. Functionally, the circle only had to show the child he could be heroic and in a moment of brilliant argument from the party, the child chooses not to open the door to heaven and exalts as a Solar (cleansing him of all it's other weird mixed powers) and the party stops the Reclamation from ever kicking off.<br /> <br /> That shit was a wild ride and I'm skipping TONS of details but it was the best 2nd Ed story I ever got to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T17:05:57-07:00","id":1407815,"title":"","content":"Well currently im working on being the first ever person to fuse the 5 types of jade into a new super-metal, so there's that.<br /> <br /> in 2e we reversed the Geomantic Heart of the poles of Air and Fire, which caused the flow of essence to break down and the world to end. The gods had to get Gaia to remake creation and the Maidens put our shenanigans in a time-bubble which they retcon-booted to the past in a way that made it so it had always happened but like 10 millenia ago.<br /> <br /> (2e specific) There was a musician who could play a harmony so dissonant that it caused people to <i>unattune</i> to artifacts. This was a bigger deal back then because in 2e attuning took an hour to do, so he opened every battle by absolutely screwing over every other combatant right out of their build. It was me. I was that guy.<br /> <br /> Oh, and another one in the &quot;you already changed the past&quot; type: we indirectly caused a non name little Realm girl to internalize the idea that violence is the only rule in the world, and we gave her a bolt of scarlet silk we found in the temple-dungeon during the adventure. Guess how that worked out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 08-12-2020, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T08:38:59-07:00","id":1407953,"title":"","content":"A second set of Lunar tattoos (in indigo) that protected them from a nasty Getimian trick that locked them into their animal forms... and also unexpectedly let them shift castes when they wanted, and opened up a few new castes. (Blood Moon = berserker/tracker, some other one I'm blanking on, and an Eclipse equivalent.)<br /> <br /> Autochthon came back. It's up in the sky like another moon except it doesn't move. It almost died and slipped into the underworld, but that got fixed because fucking no one wanted that.<br /> <br /> Merging Neptune with the lost primordial Nyx and a piece of the underworld that was her sleeping body to create a new world.<br /> <br /> Oh, and right now the endgame plan is to properly reincarnate a Neverborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T11:14:17-07:00","id":1407990,"title":"","content":"The <i>Cult of the Illuminated</i> has become the <i><b>Illuminated Order</b></i> and is vying with the Immaculate Order for Supremacy of Dogma. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T12:13:44-07:00","id":1408215,"title":"","content":"- Solars saving a region that was under attack of the biggest army in the place, led by an Abyssal, a Raksha, and a Lunar. <br /> <br /> - Same Solars destroying the same region they just saved by calling the power of the Primordial their first incarnation imprisonned in a Legendary manse because they wanted to smite their next enemy. (Was a Limit break)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}